// Replay reject pin: notation capture of the binding probe (A-1,
// 2026-07-24 second audit, CRITICAL; fix 2026-07-25; runtime row
// landed 2026-07-28 with the owed-pins batch). A user proof.lean
// declaring `notation "goal" => True` makes every later mention of
// `goal` — including the kernel-checked binding theorem — resolve in
// the USER's token table, so a proof of True would admit a false
// obligation. The lint half of the fix bans syntax-declaring
// commands in proof-side files outright
// (proof-source-lint.awk; kernel-selftest + trust-tier-selftest pin
// the lint and the «»-spelling variants); THIS row pins that the
// rejection fires end-to-end through the RUNTIME replay path — the
// wiring the lint-level cases cannot see.
enable_experimental;
fails (prove_print (offline_lean_replay "rejected_proof")
  {{ \(x : [8]) (y : [8]) -> x + y == y + x }});
